# GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and Zenodo's release archive both read this.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this template, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "project-templates"
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest release.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23701980"
abstract: >-
  A Copier template that starts Python, TypeScript, Rust, Go and Docker repos, secure by
  default and kept current by a weekly update PR. Research code comes citable, with
  CITATION.cff, a Zenodo DOI and a Software Heritage archive. Its data-pipeline kind
  builds a dataset from public sources where every row says which download it came from,
  and the web-app kind adds legal pages and an accessibility statement.
authors:
  - given-names: "Simon"
    family-names: "van Lierde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6953-909X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/simonvanlierde/project-templates"
url: "https://simonvanlierde.com/project-templates/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - copier
  - project template
  - research software
  - provenance
  - data pipeline
  - supply-chain security
  - web app
  - python
  - typescript
  - rust
  - go
  - docker
  - dependency updates
